    {
      "beat_id": "B01",
      "estimated_duration_s": 12,
      "narration_text": "This is Liam, in for Bear. You cannot copy an unknown qubit, and directly reading it destroys its superposition. Yet a quantum code can locate an error by learning only relationships — never the hidden logical state.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "CARD",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "type",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "ClaudeComposerAsk",
          "props": {
            "command": "Show how a quantum error can be found without reading the qubit.",
            "topic": "QUANTUM MECHANICS — ERROR CORRECTION",
            "segment": "Syndromes Without Secrets",
            "greeting": "Aloha, Liam",
            "runningText": "measuring parity, not logical information…",
            "output": [
              "Encode one logical qubit across three physical qubits.",
              "Read two parity checks to locate one bit flip."
            ],
            "folderLabel": "@NikBearBrown",
            "modelLabel": "Claude",
            "effortLabel": "High"
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B01.mp4",
            "at": ""
          }
        }
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B01.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 12.84,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B01.mp4",
        "filled_by": "media",
        "at": "2026-07-18T22:59:01"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B02",
      "estimated_duration_s": 11,
      "narration_text": "Take the three-qubit repetition code. The logical state alpha zero plus beta one becomes alpha zero-zero-zero plus beta one-one-one. The amplitudes remain unknown.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "branch"
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B02.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 10.77,
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B02.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim",
        "at": "2026-07-18T22:59:01"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B03",
      "estimated_duration_s": 10,
      "narration_text": "This code protects against one bit flip, an X error. It does not by itself protect against phase errors or arbitrary noise.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "threshold"
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B03.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 7.64,
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B03.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim",
        "at": "2026-07-18T22:59:01"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B04",
      "estimated_duration_s": 11,
      "narration_text": "Suppose the middle physical qubit flips. The encoded state becomes alpha zero-one-zero plus beta one-zero-one. Reading any qubit directly would leak logical information.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "transform"
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B04.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 10.62,
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B04.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim",
        "at": "2026-07-18T22:59:01"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B05",
      "estimated_duration_s": 11,
      "narration_text": "Instead, ask whether qubits one and two agree, and whether qubits two and three agree. These are parity checks, often extracted through ancillas.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "compare"
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B05.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 7.81,
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B05.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim",
        "at": "2026-07-18T22:59:01"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B06",
      "estimated_duration_s": 11,
      "narration_text": "With no error, both pairs agree: syndrome zero-zero. If qubit one flips, only the first check disagrees: one-zero.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "accumulate"
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B06.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 7.62,
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B06.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim",
        "at": "2026-07-18T22:59:01"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B07",
      "estimated_duration_s": 11,
      "narration_text": "A flip on qubit two makes both checks disagree: one-one. A flip on qubit three gives zero-one. Each single-bit error has its own two-bit address.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "accumulate"
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B07.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 9.26,
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B07.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim",
        "at": "2026-07-18T22:59:01"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B08",
      "estimated_duration_s": 11,
      "narration_text": "Crucially, the same syndrome appears for the zero-zero-zero branch and the one-one-one branch. The measurement learns where the flip occurred, not alpha or beta.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "compare"
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B08.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 9.41,
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B08.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim",
        "at": "2026-07-18T22:59:01"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B09",
      "estimated_duration_s": 10,
      "narration_text": "Syndrome one-one therefore tells the controller to apply X to qubit two. That returns the state to alpha zero-zero-zero plus beta one-one-one.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "transform"
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B09.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 9.19,
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B09.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim",
        "at": "2026-07-18T22:59:01"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B10",
      "estimated_duration_s": 12,
      "narration_text": "The trick is not measurement without disturbance. It is a carefully chosen measurement that preserves coherence inside the logical subspace while revealing which error subspace the state occupies.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "collapse"
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B10.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 11.24,
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B10.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim",
        "at": "2026-07-18T22:59:01"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B11",
      "estimated_duration_s": 12,
      "narration_text": "Your turn. Syndrome one-zero appears in this convention. Which qubit flipped, and what remains unknown? Pause before the answer: qubit one; the logical amplitudes alpha and beta remain hidden.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "CARD",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "type",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "ClaudeComposerAsk",
          "props": {
            "command": "Your turn: decode syndrome 10.",
            "topic": "QUANTUM MECHANICS — CHECK",
            "segment": "Locate, Don't Read",
            "greeting": "Over to you, Liam",
            "runningText": "waiting for the correction…",
            "output": [
              "Syndrome 10: apply X to physical qubit 1.",
              "Still unknown: logical amplitudes alpha and beta."
            ],
            "folderLabel": "@NikBearBrown",
            "modelLabel": "Claude",
            "effortLabel": "High"
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B11.mp4",
            "at": ""
          }
        }
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B11.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 11.22,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B11.mp4",
        "filled_by": "media",
        "at": "2026-07-18T22:59:01"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B12",
      "estimated_duration_s": 8,
      "narration_text": "Fixing quantum errors without looking: measure the error's fingerprint, keep the encoded secret, and reverse the diagnosed fault.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "own",
